{
  "slug": "supermarket-laser-scanner",
  "title": "Supermarket Checkout Laser Scanner",
  "year": "1974",
  "subtitle": "The glass window you swipe groceries across — object-as-input over a fixed scanning surface, the sound of checkout itself",
  "why_scout_cares": "Every other scanning exhibit in the museum is a handheld wand or a data-storage barcode. The fixed-position supermarket checkout scanner is the one where you pass a physical item over a glass window and the machine reads it — object-as-input over a fixed surface, with the iconic 'beep' of checkout. A commercially triumphant, physically ritual interaction with no near neighbor in the collection.",
  "search_terms": [
